{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Pole Acrobat: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja43'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 43 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Atthakāmavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Wanting to Help </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>3. Veḷukajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Pole Acrobat: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yo atthakāmassa hitānukampino, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One who does not follow advice when instructed </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ovajjamāno na karoti sāsanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by an ally who wants to help, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ so nihato seti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>ends up destroyed </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Veḷukassa yathā pitā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like the pole acrobat’s father. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Veḷukajātakaṁ tatiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
